{
  "note": "One case per delonix.node.v1 binding, with the backend answering the EMPTY message of that binding's response type: what varies between them is the response type, so this measures the response writer over all 56 bindings' output messages. Method, target, headers and body are the canonical request of conformance/cases/request-delonix-node-v1.json, which is where they were written by hand; the five server-streaming RPCs (WatchOperation, Logs, WatchEvents, Exec, Console) are left out \u2014 ForwardResponseStream is a later phase. The last cases add a failing backend, response metadata and trailers on top of one binding each. Three cases were tried and removed because they measure Go's transport or net/http, not the gateway: an OK status with no message (grpc-go turns it into EOF/Unknown before the gateway sees it), a negative code (grpc-status is unsigned on the wire, so the client reports \"malformed grpc-status\"), and a malformed path escape (net/http answers 400 text/plain itself, so the mux is never reached \u2014 that path is measured by conformance/cases/errors.json and path.json, which feed the mux directly).",
